---
export const prerender = false

// The POV / manifesto surface. The category argument in full: work is people and
// tools (both off the shelf), it comes back to people who leave, no single tool
// closes the gap between them, the old-way/new-way shift, employed-not-installed,
// substrate durability, and the guide. The home is the condensed version of this;
// /operator is the mechanism; this is the conviction.
//
// DRAFT COPY - directional for the Captain's voice pass. Structure is final.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import CtaButton from '../components/CtaButton.astro'
import { CATEGORY_NAME, CATEGORY_ARTICLE } from '../lib/category'

const comparison = [
  {
    label: 'How it fits',
    old: 'Off the shelf, bent to fit',
    now: 'Built for how you run',
  },
  { label: 'The budget line', old: 'Software seats, plus a salary', now: 'A worker, run for you' },
  { label: 'Ramp', old: 'Months to useful', now: 'Up to speed in a fraction of the time' },
  {
    label: 'When they leave',
    old: 'The knowledge walks out the door',
    now: 'The memory stays with the business',
  },
  {
    label: 'The work between tools',
    old: 'Falls to your people, by hand',
    now: 'Done by the worker, by design',
  },
  { label: 'Who keeps it running', old: 'You, as a second job', now: 'We do, as the service' },
  {
    label: 'What you are locked into',
    old: 'A salary, and a tool you replace',
    now: 'The role; the technology moves under it',
  },
]
---

<Base
  title={`Why ${CATEGORY_ARTICLE} ${CATEGORY_NAME} | SMD Services`}
  description="Businesses have always run on the people they hire and the tools they buy, and both come off the shelf. There is now a third option: a worker built for your business. This is the argument for it."
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" role="main">
    <!-- § 01 The thesis -->
    <section class="bg-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] px-6 pt-24 pb-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-8"
          >§ 01</span
        >
        <h1
          class="mb-10 font-['Archivo'] text-5xl md:text-7xl font-black uppercase leading-[1.02] tracking-[-0.03em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          Two Ways To Get Work Done. Now There's A Third.
        </h1>
        <div class="space-y-8 text-xl leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]">
          <p>
            Work gets done two ways: the people you hire and the tools you buy. Between them sits
            the connective work. The follow-up that has to happen, the handoff between two systems,
            the inquiry that needs a reply, the thing that falls through the crack when no one is
            watching. It holds a business together, and it has always come down to a person.
          </p>
          <p>
            There is now a third way. We call it {CATEGORY_ARTICLE}
            {CATEGORY_NAME}: not a person you hire or a tool you buy, but a worker built for your
            business and run for you.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- § 02 What the seat costs: it always comes back to people, who leave -->
    <section class="bg-white px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-4"
          >§ 02</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-10 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          What The Seat Really Costs.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]">
          <p>
            Businesses have hired people to do this work since the dawn of business, and the trouble
            with it is universal. The seat empties and you start over. A new hire takes months to
            become useful, and you pay full salary for partial value the whole time.
          </p>
          <p>
            What they learn about how you run lives in their head, and the day they leave, it leaves
            with them. The cost is fixed and rising whether the work is full or slow. And the people
            you most want on the real work spend their day stitching together tools that should talk
            to each other and do not.
          </p>
          <p>
            None of this is a failure of the people or the owner. It is the shape of the job. The
            job is real, the work is necessary, and doing it with people and tools that were never
            built for your business is the problem.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- § 03 The work lives between the tools (connective tissue, tools honored) -->
    <section class="bg-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-4"
          >§ 03</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-10 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          The Work Lives Between The Tools.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]">
          <p>
            Every tool you run does a piece of the work. The practice system, the books, the
            scheduler, the inbox. Each one is good at its own job, and only as good as the person
            using it. None of them does the work that lives between them, because that work was
            never inside any single tool to begin with.
          </p>
          <p>
            So the connective work falls to a person, and you buy more tools, and the person has
            more seams to hold together. The more systems you run, the bigger that job gets. That is
            why another app has never fixed it. The fix is not a better tool. It is the thing that
            works across all of them.
          </p>
          <p>
            Which means the systems you already run are not competition. They are what the Operator
            connects. The more of them you have, the more an Operator is worth.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- § 04 Old way vs new way -->
    <section class="bg-white px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-4"
          >§ 04</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-12 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          The Old Way, And The New One.
        </h2>

        <div class="border-t-[3px] border-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]">
          <div
            class="hidden md:grid grid-cols-12 gap-0 border-b-[3px] border-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] bg-[color:var(--ss-color-background)]"
          >
            <div
              class="col-span-4 p-4 font-['Archivo_Narrow'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]"
            >
            </div>
            <div
              class="col-span-4 p-4 font-['Archivo_Narrow'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]"
            >
              The Old Way
            </div>
            <div
              class="col-span-4 p-4 font-['Archivo_Narrow'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-primary)]"
            >
              The New Way
            </div>
          </div>
          {
            comparison.map((row) => (
              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-0 border-b-[3px] border-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]">
                <div class="md:col-span-4 p-4 font-['Archivo'] text-base font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.01em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]">
                  {row.label}
                </div>
                <div class="md:col-span-4 p-4 font-['Archivo'] text-base leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)] md:border-l-[3px] md:border-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]">
                  <span class="md:hidden font-['Archivo_Narrow'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-muted)] block mb-1">
                    Old way
                  </span>
                  {row.old}
                </div>
                <div class="md:col-span-4 p-4 font-['Archivo'] text-base leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] md:border-l-[3px] md:border-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]">
                  <span class="md:hidden font-['Archivo_Narrow'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-primary)] block mb-1">
                    New way
                  </span>
                  {row.now}
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- § 05 Employed, not installed -->
    <section class="bg-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-4"
          >§ 05</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-10 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          Employed, Not Installed.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]">
          <p>
            A tool is something you buy and then run. A worker is something you hire and put to
            work. The Operator is the second kind. You are not adding a line to your software bill.
            You are taking on the work a person would do.
          </p>
          <p>
            So the honest comparison is not against other software. It is against what it costs to
            put a person on this work, fully loaded, and keep them there. We price it against that,
            and we walk through it with you before anything is built.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- § 06 The substrate moves; the role stays -->
    <section class="bg-white px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-4"
          >§ 06</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-10 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          The Technology Moves. The Role Stays.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]">
          <p>
            This field changes every month. The biggest fear in buying anything built on it is
            simple: what if you bet on the wrong thing and it is behind by next year.
          </p>
          <p>
            You are not betting on our stack. You hired the role. When something better comes along
            underneath, moving you to it is our job, not yours, and what the Operator has learned
            about your business comes with it. The worker stays. The memory stays. The technology it
            runs on is ours to keep current.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- § 07 The guide is the point -->
    <section class="bg-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-4"
          >§ 07</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-10 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          A Team, Not A Download.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]">
          <p>
            The Operator does not show up out of a box. A person on our team sits with you, learns
            how your business actually runs, and builds the worker around it. That person stays with
            the engagement, watches how it performs, and keeps it sharp.
          </p>
          <p>
            That is the part that does not come from anywhere else. Anyone can stand up a generic
            agent. The worker that is built well for your business, run by a team that stays
            accountable for it, and a memory that gets deeper the longer it runs, is the thing worth
            hiring.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- § 08 Start the conversation -->
    <section class="bg-[color:var(--ss-color-surface-inverse)] px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl text-center">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-8"
          >§ 08</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-6 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-white"
        >
          Start The Conversation.
        </h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mb-10 max-w-2xl text-lg text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-muted)]">
          We learn how your operation runs, find the work that is eating your team's time, and
          figure out where a dedicated Operator fits. If the fit is not right, we say so.
        </p>
        <CtaButton variant="outline-white" href="/book?interest=operator" data-ev="why-final-cta"
          >Start the conversation</CtaButton
        >
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
